All referenced Linux driver sources use GPL-2.0-or-later. Source URLs and
SHA-256 hashes are recorded in references/linux-sources.json. The manifest
records research paths; the upstream source files are not vendored here.
The macOS adaptation replaces Linux device/V4L2/URB infrastructure with
userspace IOKit requests, bounded initialization, a control rollback journal,
and asynchronous isochronous transfers. It is not a Linux kernel module.

The SAV/EAV parser uses the cx231xx-video.c protocol as a technical reference.
No firmware image, vendor driver binary or captured media is distributed.

Windows timestamp encoder: references/ffmpeg/vhsts.c (LGPL-2.1-or-later) adapts
the user's vhs-recorder-tool packet transport with UYVY/525-line support. The
separate FFmpeg build reuses that project's MPEG-2 precision/MPEG-PS PTS fixes.
Build recipe, source pin and corresponding sources: tools/build_timestamp_ffmpeg.py
and references/ffmpeg. This encoder does not replace the system FFmpeg.
